xnu 0432: delay the automatic W6 load so the USB ring is up

The automatic W6 load runs at W4. On the skip-all builds W4 happens before the
USB control channel serves the ring, so a crash inside the load leaves no
ring to read. `mondrianwifidelay=<ms>` delays the load (default 20000 ms); the
ring then carries the W6 lines and a panic can be read with `prev`.

The delay is bounded to 60 s and applies only to the automatic load; `wififw`
and `wifibhi` stay immediate.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
index 5fd40ea..25d5e6e 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -1401,6 +1401,7 @@ mondrian_wifi_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 {
 	int ok = wifi_cold_link() == 0;
 	int autoload = 0;
+	int delay_ms = 20000;
 
 	/*
 	 * W6: the USB command races the worker, and on a cold boot the rail
@@ -1410,6 +1411,14 @@ mondrian_wifi_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 	 */
 	if (ok && PE_parse_boot_argn("mondrianwififw", &autoload,
 	    sizeof(autoload)) && autoload != 0) {
+		if (!PE_parse_boot_argn("mondrianwifidelay", &delay_ms,
+		    sizeof(delay_ms))) {
+			delay_ms = 20000;
+		}
+		if (delay_ms > 0 && delay_ms < 60000) {
+			wifi_log("W6 auto load delay %d ms", delay_ms);
+			delay(delay_ms * 1000);
+		}
 		wifi_log("W6 auto load start");
 		(void)mondrian_wifi_load_amss();
 	}
